    "summary": "SPF measures how well sunscreen blocks UVB rays, but the protection gains above SPF 50 are minimal. For most people, SPF 30 broad-spectrum sunscreen applied generously and reapplied regularly is sufficient, with SPF 50 recommended for prolonged or intense sun exposure.",
